# /etc/sudoers.d/blackbox-system
# Generated by BlackBox install.sh — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
#
# Grants the BlackBox service user passwordless sudo for a TIGHTLY BOUNDED
# set of system operations. The grant itself is the security perimeter:
# any prompt-injection RCE through an MCP tool can ONLY invoke commands
# listed here. The dispatch helpers (/usr/local/sbin/blackbox-{apt-install,
# write-systemd}) add a second layer of validation but the perimeter is
# already this file.
#
# History:
#   - E1   : initial Tailscale wizard grants
#   - E2   : NoNewPrivileges=false in unit (required for sudo escalation
#            despite the bounded grants; container-style hardening alone)
#   - E22a : service-restart + journalctl grants for portal restart+logs
#   - T5   : renamed -tailscale → -system; added update-pipeline grants
#            via /usr/local/sbin/blackbox-* dispatch helpers (T2). Audit
#            C3 + C4 ruled out wildcard `apt-get install -y *` and
#            `tee /etc/sudoers.d/*` as priv-esc primitives.
#   - 2026-10 audit rank 17 (X04-security-clients-infra-02): NO grant ends in
#            a glob. sudoers matches the arguments as ONE space-joined string,
#            so a trailing `*` also matched any extra root-run flags. Every
#            grant is now exact arguments or an anchored `^…$` regex
#            (sudo >= 1.9.10; install-preflight.sh pins Ubuntu 24.04 = 1.9.15.
#            An older sudo either rejects this file at visudo -c or never
#            matches those grants: both fail closed, and install.sh warns).
#            The journalctl grant is gone (the service reads
#            its journal as a systemd-journal member) and so is the unused
#            zellij binary helper. Pinned by
#            scripts/tests/test_sudoers_template_perimeter.sh (golden list).

# ── Tailscale wizard actuator (E1) ──────────────────────────────────────
# `up` and `cert` carry one variable token each, so they are anchored regexes
# over the WHOLE argument string — exactly the shape tailscale_actuator.py
# builds and nothing more (no --login-server / --ssh / --auth-key on `up`, no
# --cert-file / --key-file output paths on `cert`):
#   up --accept-dns=true --hostname=<_safe_hostname(): one DNS label>
#   cert <Self.DNSName: dot-separated labels ending in .ts.net>
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/apt-get install -y tailscale
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale ^up --accept-dns=true --hostname=[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale set --accept-dns=true
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale ^cert [a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?(\.[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?)*\.ts\.net$
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale serve --bg --https=443 9091
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale serve status --json
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale serve reset
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale logout
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start tailscaled
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl enable tailscaled

# ── Service control (E22a) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The former `journalctl -u blackbox.service *` grant ran journalctl as root
# with ANY extra arguments (--vacuum-*, --rotate, --file/--directory reads).
# install.sh now adds the service user to the systemd-journal group, and
# /onboarding/logs/stream runs plain `journalctl` — no root involved.
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart blackbox.service

# ── MCP remote server one-click onboarding (M7.4) ───────────────────────
# Funnel-up exposes the local MCP HTTP server (127.0.0.1:9093) on the PUBLIC
# internet at :8443. Port-only `9093` (NOT http://127.0.0.1:9093) mirrors the
# `serve` grant above and avoids an unescaped `:` in sudoers grammar. The
# onboarding route gates funnel-up behind an explicit user confirmation.
# These are all /etc-FREE runtime ops (tailscaled socket + PID-1 transitions);
# the unit INSTALL+enable is installer-time (writes /etc, blocked by
# ProtectSystem=strict in the service namespace) -- deliberately NOT granted here.
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale funnel --bg --https=8443 9093
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale funnel status --json
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tailscale funnel reset
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start blackbox-mcp.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart blackbox-mcp.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl stop blackbox-mcp.service

# ── Update pipeline (T5) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are the ONLY grants needed for the update pipeline. Each helper
# script validates its arguments before doing anything destructive:
#
#   blackbox-apt-install <pkg>
#     - regex-checks <pkg> against ^[a-z0-9.+-]+$
#     - verifies <pkg> is in Scripts/onboarding/system-packages.txt allowlist
#     - then: apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends <pkg>
#
#   blackbox-write-systemd <target_kind>
#     - takes NO caller-supplied source (install.sh-grant removal, 2026-07-27):
#       copies the RENDERED, root-owned /etc/blackbox/templates/<target_kind>
#       to the kind's hardcoded destination. Caller controls neither the
#       destination NOR the content of any privileged write.
#     - target_kind whitelisted (unit | override | cli-agent-overrides |
#       zellij-web-unit | …-helper | sudoers-system | asterisk-* | …)
#     - destination is HARDCODED per target_kind (caller cannot pick path)
#     - sudoers-* targets validated by `visudo -c` BEFORE copy
#     - systemd targets trigger daemon-reload after write
#
# A prompt-injection RCE cannot abuse these to install arbitrary packages,
# write arbitrary sudoers rules, or escalate beyond the dispatcher's
# narrow purpose. That's the design intent — the helpers ARE the policy.
#
# The grants no longer end in `*` (2026-10 audit rank 17): sudo itself bounds
# the arguments before the helper sees them. apt-install takes exactly ONE
# package-name token that cannot start with `-` (no option injection); the
# allowlist check stays in the helper. write-systemd is granted ONLY the kinds
# install.sh publishes to the trusted store (publish_template_store's
# STORE_MANIFEST) — every other kind would fail closed (exit 6) anyway — and
# with exactly one argument, so the legacy ignored second argument is refused.
# Adding a store kind means adding its grant line here in the same commit.
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/blackbox-apt-install ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.+-]*$
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/blackbox-write-systemd sudoers-system
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/blackbox-write-systemd apt-install-helper
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/blackbox-write-systemd write-systemd-helper
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/blackbox-write-systemd zellij-web-unit

# ── Update-pipeline systemd regen (install.sh-grant removal, 2026-07-27) ─
# The former `NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/bash <root>/Scripts/install.sh` grant lived
# here. It was the ONE in-service→arbitrary-root escalation: any prompt-
# injection RCE in the service could `sudo -n bash install.sh` and run the
# whole installer as root. It is DELETED. The update pipeline's system-level
# regen (Orchestrator/update/runner.py::_privileged_regen) now dispatches the
# individual bounded blackbox-write-systemd target_kinds below for each CHANGED
# git-tracked template instead of re-running install.sh. New system packages
# and genuinely new always-on units remain a one-time operator `sudo bash
# install.sh` step — see docs/runbooks/2026-07-27-remove-install-sh-grant.md.

# ── Zellij CLI Agent (Track A T4, audit C5) ─────────────────────────────
# Grants required by the Zellij rewrite of the CLI Agent terminal stack.
# Plan: docs/plans/2026-05-24-zellij-cli-agent-rewrite.md (Track A).
#
# Why two grants and not just `restart`:
#   - `systemctl restart zellij-web.service` — normal lifecycle (rotate
#     binary, recover from a hung session, post-update bounce).
#   - `systemctl daemon-reload` — REQUIRED whenever the unit file content
#     on disk changes (e.g. update pipeline writes a new
#     zellij-web.service via blackbox-write-systemd). `restart` alone does
#     NOT re-read the unit; systemd will keep running the old definition
#     until daemon-reload. These are separate sudo verbs, hence two grants.
#     NOTE: this grant is general-purpose — any future unit added via
#     blackbox-write-systemd benefits from it; do NOT duplicate this rule
#     in future sections (e.g. a hypothetical worker.service grant block).
#
# The former `/usr/local/sbin/blackbox-install-zellij-binary *` grant is
# DELETED (2026-10 audit X04-security-clients-infra-01): nothing called it,
# and it compared the caller's version against a pin file inside the
# service-writable repo, fetched the expected sha256 from the download origin,
# then ran the result as root. The zellij binary is installed (and a pin bump
# applied) only by the human-run `sudo bash install.sh` (Step 2c), which also
# removes the deployed helper.
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart zellij-web.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl daemon-reload

# ── Local model stack (local-model-stack M2) ────────────────────────────
# blackbox-models.service is the llama-swap front door (:9098) supervising
# the on-box STT/TTS/embeddings/rerank members. `restart` is normal lifecycle
# (config regen on update, hung-member recovery, post-update bounce); `stop`
# is used by the Phase-2 MS02 migration. daemon-reload is already granted
# above (general-purpose) and unit INSTALL+enable is installer-time root.
#
# The Phase-2 Step-0 reset must RETIRE the pre-stack always-resident pair
# before the retrieval group can first load (a pointer flip alone leaves the
# keep_alive=-1-pinned ~7GB Ollama 8B resident → CUDA OOM at the re-embed):
# stop vllm-reranker.service AND ollama to free VRAM. These are /etc-free
# runtime PID-1 transitions; exact-command grants keep the perimeter tight.
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart blackbox-models.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl stop blackbox-models.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl disable --now vllm-reranker.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl stop vllm-reranker.service
REAL_USER_PLACEHOLDER ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl stop ollama.service
